## Why this works
- 06 (partial names): single-token headwords map 1:1 to Wiktionary entries; there is no name-scope to match.
- 08 (wrong name / birth name): we look up the token itself, not a scraped lead that transcribes a nearby name.
- 09 (scientific name): "beetle" is looked up directly; scientific names only appear if kept as candidates (we can drop/flag them).
- 10 (mechanical artifacts): kaikki JSONL is structured (`sounds[].ipa`), no wikitext comment / `,_` cruft.
- 07 (alt pronunciations): collapses to "first `sounds[].ipa` with `lang=en`".

## Source decision: kaikki.org dump over live API (recommended)
- kaikki.org English postprocessed JSONL ≈ **3.2 GB** compressed, 1,396,111 headwords,
  extracted 2026-10-21 from the 2026-10-01 enwiktionary dump via wiktextract. Entries carry
  `word`, `lang`/`lang_code`, `pos`, `forms`, `etymology`, and per-pronunciation `sounds[]`
  with `ipa`. Caveat: that postprocessed page says "DEPRECATED, will be removed"; pin the
  raw wiktextract JSONL URL as the durable source before building.
- Live API: no hard per-request quota (standard MediaWiki `maxlag=5`), but bulk crawling is
  against etiquette and returns un-structured `{{IPA}}` templates you'd re-parse by hand.
  For an offline-pipeline → DB-artifact, the dump is the right dependency; the API can remain
  an optional incremental fallback.
- **>2 GB rule:** this exceeds AGENTS.md's 2 GB download threshold, so I need an explicit
  go-ahead, and it would be staged under the gitignored `resources/`.

## Tokenization tradeoff (your call)
Single-word tokenization loses true multi-word pronunciations ("New Orleans" → "NOO OR-lənz",
"Al Pacino" → surname only). Recommended default: tokenize to single words as primary BUT
also probe whether the whole phrase is itself a Wiktionary headword (many proper nouns are)
and prefer the full-phrase entry when present — recovers most names at zero cost. Confirmed
decision needed from you: phrase-passthrough yes/no.

## Lookup / first-IPA policy (deterministic)
1. Normalize token (lowercase; diacritic-stripped fallback).
2. Match headword; prefer exact `lang_code=en`.
3. Take first English `sounds[].ipa`, skipping empty/audio-only.
4. Homographs ("lead", "bow"): prefer etymology 1 by default; region preference (GenAm vs RP) as a later config.
5. Feed the IPA through the existing `respell.ipa_to_canonical_respell` — the converter stays reusable.

